  "question": "In which situations should base quality score recalibration be disabled in Sarek, and which Control-FREEC output file lists beta allele frequencies?",
  "answer": "Base quality score recalibration should be turned off when the reads are UMI tagged or when DragMap is used as the mapper [sarek_output#h017]. It is also not needed for every tool combination in Sarek [sarek_output#h017].\nThe Control-FREEC file that lists beta allele frequencies is the BAF text file: <tumorsample>_BAF.txt for tumor-only samples, and <tumorsample_vs_normalsample>.mpileup.gz_BAF.txt for tumor/normal pairs. It contains the beta allele frequency for each possibly heterozygous SNP position [sarek_output#h049].",
