  "question": "Як DeepVariant визначає варіанти та що відбувається з його викликами далі?",
  "answer": "DeepVariant is a variant caller based on deep learning. It takes aligned reads, produces pileup image tensors from them, classifies each tensor with a convolutional neural network, and reports the results in a standard VCF or gVCF file [rare_output#h015].\nIts calls are joint genotyped with GLnexus and then normalized with bcftools norm [rare_output#h015]. By default, only the normalized VCF files are placed in the output folder [rare_output#h015]. In a separate mitochondrial analysis, mitochondrial calls are filtered from the normalized VCFs with GATK SelectVariants before they are published [rare_output#h015].\nIn Sarek, DeepVariant results for normal samples are written to {outdir}/variant_calling/deepvariant/<sample>/ as VCF and gVCF files with tabix indexes [sarek_output#h027].",
